  "story": {
    "day": 163,
    "title": "Kaya's Camp Night",
    "sentences": [
      "Kaya spent a rainy day at a public camp.",
      "Her father, age forty, showed her a little rope.",
      "They went hiking and tried to climb a small hill.",
      "She saw white sheep and a wild horse there.",
      "At 7 p.m., Dad began to boil water for spaghetti.",
      "\"I'll add one ounce of cabbage and lettuce,\" he said.",
      "He quickly put in a tablespoon of sauce.",
      "\"You'll love such a dinner!\" he laughed. Kaya didn't answer.",
      "For dessert, she ate pudding, not thinking of steak.",
      "She didn't feel sad or think about wolves, nor skiing.",
      "A million stars appeared; she took off her shoes.",
      "\"He'll teach calligraphy the day after tomorrow,\" she looked forward with attention."
    ]
  }
}